mes>S.D</given-names></name><name><surname>Guinness</surname><given-names>F.E</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Parental investment in male and female offspring in polygynous mammals</article-title><source>Nature</source><volume>289</volume><year>1981</year><fpage>487</fpage><lpage>489</lpage><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://dx.doi.org/doi:10.1038/289487a0">doi:10.1038/289487a0</ext-link></citation></ref><ref id="bib9"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>C&#x000f4;t&#x000e9;</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Blanchard</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Lalumi&#x000e8;re</surname><given-names>M.L</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The influence of birth order on birth weight: does the sex of preceding siblings matter?</article-title><source>J. Biosoc. Sci</source><volume>35</volume><year>2003</year><fpage>455</fpage><lpage>462</lpage><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://dx.doi.org/doi:10.1017/S0021932003004553">doi:10.1017/S0021932003004553</ext-link><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12887223</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib10"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Drent</surname><given-names>R.H</given-names></name><name><surname>Daan</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The prudent parent: energetic adjustments in avian breeding</article-title><source>Ardea</source><volume>68</volume><year>1980</year><fpage>225</fpage><lpage>252</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="bib11"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Festa-Bianchet</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Individual differences, parasites, and the costs of reproduction for bighorn ewes (<italic>Ovis canadensis</italic>)</article-title><source>J. Anim. Ecol</source><volume>58</volume><year>1989</year><fpage>785</fpage><lpage>795</lpage><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://dx.doi.org/doi:10.2307/5124">doi:10.2307/5124</ext-link></citation></ref><ref id="bib12"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Festa-Bianchet</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Jorgenson</surname><given-names>J.T</given-names></name><name><surname>R&#x000e9;ale</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Early development, adult mass and reproductive success in bighorn sheep</article-title><source>Behav. Ecol</source><volume>11</volume><year>2000</year><fpage>633</fpage><lpage>639</lpage><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://dx.doi.org/doi:10.1093/beheco/11.6.633">doi:10.1093/beheco/11.6.633</ext-link></citation></ref><ref id="bib13"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Gomendio</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Clutton-Brock</surname><given-names>T.H</given-names></name><name><surname>Albon</surname><given-names>S.D</given-names></name><name><surname>Guinness</surname><given-names>F.E</given-names></name><name><surname>Simpson</surname><given-names>M.J</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Mammalian sex ratios and variation in costs of rearing sons and daughters</article-title><source>Nature</source><volume>343</volume><year>1990</year><fpage>261</fpage><lpage>263</lpage><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://dx.doi.org/doi:10.1038/343261a0">doi:10.1038/343261a0</ext-link><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2300169</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib14"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Gustafsson</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Sutherland</surname><given-names>W.J</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The costs of reproduction in the collared flycatcher <italic>Fi